            <div xml:id="d71">

                <pb facs="0078" n="66" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg66"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">883.00/1234: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-02-04T11:00:00+02:00">February 4,
                            1942—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 4:07 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>196. My 188, February 2 [<hi rendition="#italic">3</hi>], 6 p.m. The King
                    conferred with the leaders of the various parties yesterday afternoon. Nahas
                    Pasha, the Wafd leader, was received first and I am confidentially informed that
                    the King suggested to him the formation of a coalition Cabinet but that Nahas
                    took the position that the situation was so serious that he could only assume
                    responsibility for government if given a free hand to form a Wafd Cabinet. I am
                    further advised that the British Ambassador saw the Chief of the Royal Cabinet
                    last night and without taking a stand on the coalition Government issue made it
                    clear that he must insist on Nahas being given an opportunity to form a
                    government in accordance with Nahas wishes.</p>
                <p>It is reported that the King is continuing his conversations today.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
